I've just had a damned annoying death.

(spoiler warning of sorts)


I finally got down to level 51, found the vibrating square and 
thought "Yeah!"  Ok, so I loaded the candelabrum, rung the bell
and read the book.  Nothing happened.  Confusion set in.  Then
I read the message about the runes being scrambled and me being
unable to read them.  Was it because my Barbarian had an Int of
5?  No, I thought cos thats high for barbarians so they'd be
stuffed. ;)

It must be cursed!  (bear with me...this is the first time I've
had a probelm with the Book of the Dead).  Ok, I thought, I
have no scrolls of remove curse and there were no ready magic
traps around (besides the wizard was loose and I didn't want to
stuff around much just to get more stuff cursed).  Time to reach
deep into the Blessed Bag of Holding.  I pulled out that magic
marker and my last (sob) potion of water.  Then I didpped one of
the (many) scrolls of teleportation I'd found, wrote on the 
unlabeled scroll and hey presto the book was soon uncursed.

It was at this time the wizard decided it was time to attack
again *sigh*.  I thwacked him a few times, teleported next to
the upstairs and beat him up severely.  Unfortunately he'd 
"Double Troubled" (tm) himself and managed to curse a few items.
I could live with it.  Back to the vibrating square.  Relight
the candelabrum, ring the bell and read the book.  He'd cursed
it again!  AAAAARRRRRGGGGGGHHHHH!!!!!!!!

No time to panic!  Think, I thought, think.  I grabbed all my
scrolls and used a precious charge from my wand of polymorph.
Lo and behold I got an unlabeled scroll!  We're back in business.
Thank God (Crom?) for that magic marker...

All went well.  I thwacked the priests, found my way to the high
priest and zapped him with a wand of death (I hate critters that
curse my stuff), grabbed the amulet and inscribed it with
"The Real Thing (tm)" ;)  Now comes the long trek back up.

That also went fairly well.  Only a couple of encounters with the
wizard.  I'd put on my ring of levitation to avoid all those
annoying trapdoors hidden under piles of items that littered
Gehennom (and everywhere else for that matter).  Unfortunately
in one of my encounters with the wizard he'd cursed the bloody
thing!  Not a problem (well, not much anyway).  I'll just make
my way out of Gehennom and pray to get it off.

Or so I thought.  Around level 37 I took the wrong upstairs and 
ended up in Vlad's tower.  Bugger!  There was no way out of this.
I couldn't polypile as I couldn't reach the items.  I couldn't
grab items out of my bag (for the same reasons).  Nor could I
sit on the throne (in the hope of a wish) or hope to find 
something that might help (since I couldn't pick it up) *sigh*.

Desperate times call for desperate measures.  I kept on zapping
myself with the wand of polymorph in the hope of something
that might get me out of this situation.  Sure my cursed bits of
armor fell off (another legacy from my encounters with the wizard)
but no such luck with the rings.  I couldn't think of anything
else.

Oh well.  And thus ends another frustrating game of Nethack.

"Does this post have a point?" I hear you ask.  "Not really!" but
I'll continue anyway. :)  Enough of my ramblings and now to a
couple of questions and comments.

Is there any way out of my predicament?  Was there a form that
I couldn't polymorphed into that would've made the rings fall
off?  I know that in an older version of Nethack (pre 3.0j)
cursed boots of levitation eventually fell off.  Is this the
case in 3.1.2?  Is this the case with cursed rings of levitation?
It didn't seem so to me, I'd had it on for quite awhile.

If there was no way out this strikes me as being too nasty.  I
couldn't carry some emergency scrolls of remove curse because of
the prolific nature of fire traps (the nasty sort being those
that get hidden under items).  Speaking of which, traps in 
general and stairs that get hidden under items are damned
annoying.  Maybe the dev team should add a keystroke that will
tell you where all the stairs/traps (including magic portals)
are located on that level.  This might seem like its making it
too easy for the player but I don't think it is.  If the trap
or stair isn't covered with an item you can query it with the ;
key so why shouldn't you be able to do the same with those
covered with items?  Maybe theres a feature like this that I've
managed to miss.  Anyone?

Back to the ring.  I was entirely capable of making it out if
it wasn't for the fact that I'd wandered into Vlad's tower so I
feel sorta cheated.  So sue me.

One more thing.  I don't know if anyone else has mentioned it
but I'll assume they have but I'll go ahead and mention it
anyway. :)

Once you kill the wizard he should stay dead.  Having to kill
him over and over again is tedious and often trivial because of
the power level you've reached to make it this far.  Personally
I think this aspect of the game adds nothing to it.  I don't
think it really makes the game more worthwhile.  The only
difficulty it adds is in the cursing of items which is very
frustrating because of its repetitive nature and the fact that
there is nothing you can do about this (you can, sometimes with
difficulty remove the curses themselves but you can't do anything
about the source).  Also, the fact that you have to trudge back
up through 50 levels (level teleports being disabled by having
the amulet et al) is also extremely tedious.

Don't get me wrong.  I really enjoy playing nethack but the
so-called "endgame" I find extremely boring.  If I'm in the
minority then so be it but I think theres a lot of other people
that also find this stage boring.  If so, is there any chance
of some sort of change to the endgame?  I do appreciate the
effort the dev team has put into making the game more interesting
but I don't think this is the way to do it (IMHO of course).

Anyway, happy hacking and its goodnight from me


